. LESSON 5 STORING MACROS ON TAPE AND DISK
. In these examples color 1 is teal, not red. $L1 says which of the
. palette's 256 colors color 1 shows (lesson 7); 29 is teal, and
. $L1=1 makes it red again.
$L1=29
. There is no cassette or disk here, so this lesson's commands, PUTTAPE,
. GETTAPE, DSETUP, DINIT, DS, DPUT, DGET, DCREATE and DUSEMAP, aren't
. emulated. The GRASS node's buttons do their job instead:
.   Save .grass writes every macro, variable and array to a file, as
.   PUTTAPE and DPUT did. Load .grass resets the module and runs a
.   file, defining what it holds again, as GETTAPE and DGET did, but
.   with memory cleared first.
.
. USEMAP lists what is in memory, which Save would write out.
USEMAP

. SPOKES turns a reel's three spokes from angle OLD to ANG. A macro run
. by another macro gets its arguments from INPUT. The spokes are XOR,
. colormode 7, so drawing a spoke again takes it off: each new spoke is
. drawn, then its old one again. With F 0 there are no old ones yet.
SPOKES=[INPUT RX,ANG,OLD,F
LINE RX,15,4;LINE RX+28*COS(ANG),15+24*SIN(ANG),7;IF F,LINE RX,15,4;LINE RX+28*COS(OLD),15+24*SIN(OLD),7
LINE RX,15,4;LINE RX+28*COS(ANG+120),15+24*SIN(ANG+120),7;IF F,LINE RX,15,4;LINE RX+28*COS(OLD+120),15+24*SIN(OLD+120),7
LINE RX,15,4;LINE RX+28*COS(ANG+240),15+24*SIN(ANG+240),7;IF F,LINE RX,15,4;LINE RX+28*COS(OLD+240),15+24*SIN(OLD+240),7]

. THE ANIMATION. TAPE plays a cassette. Both reels turn, the full one
. slower than the empty one, a step a frame, as WAIT 1 waits for the
. next. The hub is a plain box drawn over the spokes each step.
. The node's Stop button stops it, and Play carries on.
TAPE=[CLEAR;A=0;B=0;F=0
BOX 0,0,290,180,1;BOX 0,0,280,170,0
BOX 0,-62,120,26,1;BOX 0,-62,110,18,0;BOX 0,-62,24,10,3
R=31
CIRCLE -70,15,R*7/6,R,2;IF (R=R+1)<40,SKIP 0
R=31
CIRCLE 70,15,R*7/6,R,2;IF (R=R+1)<33,SKIP 0
LINE -70,-24,4;LINE 0,-57,2;LINE 70,-18,2
1TURN SPOKES -70,A,A+5,F;BOX -70,15,13,11,3
SPOKES 70,B,B+9,F;BOX 70,15,13,11,3
F=1;A=A-5;B=B-9;WAIT 1;GOTO 1TURN]
TAPE
